Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 02:44:51 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1135/1178] The Engine page in Viktor's rows; About in three
 columns under two marks (1166, part fifteen)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Viktor 04.10.2026: «По колонкам в Engine. Давай подумаем, как всё ужать и передвинуть, чтобы на
1080p всё встало красиво и не таким длинным полотенцем… Ты всё замерь и пересмотри». From 1400px
wide one grid of thirty columns, so thirds, fifths and sixths share it: Server over Hardware
beside the log (1/3 · 2/3, the log filling its height), Compute | GPUs (2/5 · 3/5), Appearance |
Writer (4/6 · 2/6), VAEs | LoRAs (1/6 · 5/6, the decoders one under another), Sliders, About.
The cards stand in that order in the source (each with an eg-* place), so the keys walk the rows
as they are seen; narrower, the flex rows as before, `order` keeping their old sequence.
Measured at 1920×1080: the page 3 975 → 3 187 px; About 967 → 633.

About (his word: «не две горизонтальные секции там, а одна с тремя колонками RUACH STUDIO |
YuE2 + ggml + yue2.cpp | Sound decoders, Sliders, Loras. В колонке YuE2 — логотип так же, как в
первой наш»): one band of three columns with a thin line between them: ours with the layout it
took after (YuE2_WebUI); YuE2, yue2.cpp and ggml under YuE2's own mark, traced from M-A-P's logo
he downloaded (inline, 17.8 KB; the word in the theme's ink, the circle and the ² terracotta);
the add-ons. The two logos one height, the columns level under them. A narrow card stacks them.
The page test follows: the rows by their thirtieths, the three columns and the two marks.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
